NAME
    echo - print arguments

SYNOPSIS
    echo <text...>

DESCRIPTION
    Prints its arguments back, joined by single spaces - real argument
    quoting applies ('echo 'a b'' is one argument, not two). Ignores stdin
    entirely, matching real echo. Its real use is scripting: a marker line
    in a source'd script, or the natural pipeline source for a text filter
    ('echo <text> | sed s/.../.../ ').

EXAMPLES
    echo hello world
    echo $X
